User Flow — Text and Coding
A User Flow describes the sequence of steps a user follows to complete a task in a system.

For example, for an Online Shopping System:

User Flow in Text
START
  |
  v
Open Website
  |
  v
Login / Register
  |
  +---- Existing User ----> Login
  |
  +---- New User ---------> Register
                              |
                              v
                            Login
                              |
                              v
                    Browse Products
                              |
                              v
                       Select Product
                              |
                              v
                       Add to Cart
                              |
                              v
                       View Cart
                              |
                              v
                     Proceed to Checkout
                              |
                              v
                    Enter Delivery Address
                              |
                              v
                      Select Payment
                              |
                              v
                       Place Order
                              |
                              v
                     Payment Successful?
                       /             \
                     No               Yes
                     |                 |
                     v                 v
                Retry Payment     Order Confirmed
                                       |
                                       v
                                Track Order
                                       |
                                       v
                                      END

